PARTS = [('I', 'Resolution and free dynamics', 'Exact packet algebra becomes field dynamics only after reconstruction, completion, and domain control are supplied. The argument moves from finite transfers to a torus Hamiltonian and then identifies its full unitary group.', [entry('Physics_Foundations_Monograph', 'Projectors, Packets, and Transfer', 'Resolution, conservation, and operator reconstruction'), entry('Physics_Dirac_Monograph', 'Fourier Packets and the Continuum Dirac Operator', 'Clifford matrices, Fourier completion, and the exact domain'), entry('Block50_Spectral_Generator_Bridge', 'The Dirac Group and Its Generator', 'Spectral evolution, resolvents, and regularity-dependent rates')]), ('II', 'Gauge transport and gravity', 'A compatible link law is not yet a coupled field evolution. Gauge transport introduces ordered paths and curvature. Gravity adds dynamical geometry, constraints, boundary conditions, and a distinct continuum comparison.', [entry('Physics_Gauge_Monograph', 'Gauge Covariance and Geometric Refinement', 'Ordered transport, conservation, and curvature estimates'), entry('Physics_Gravity_Monograph', 'Constrained Gravity and Strong Fields', 'Canonical structure, local reduction, and spherical tests')]), ('III', 'Arithmetic and polyphase refinement', 'Arithmetic registers provide another exact resolution of a quantum state. Compatibility determines when refinement preserves the dynamics. Eliminating hidden channels produces self-energy and memory, while infinite depth requires its own analytic domain.', [entry('Physics_Adic_Monograph', 'Adic and Polyphase Quantum Refinement', 'Haar packets, spectral reduction, and infinite hierarchies')]), ('IV', 'Matter and cosmological transport', 'A mathematical refinement fiber becomes a physical proposal only after a coupling and production history are specified. The energy-budget obstruction is examined before the distribution is propagated through cosmological observables.', [entry('Projector_Refinement_Physics_Covariant_Backreaction_Bridge', 'Covariant Refinement-Fiber Dynamics', 'Symmetry, stress exchange, production, and ultraviolet bounds', (0, 30)), entry('Projector_Refinement_Physics_Volume_II', 'Cosmology, Dark Sectors, and Structure Formation', 'Conditional transport, structure, and linked rejection tests', (0, 142))]), ('V', 'Visual studies', 'The figures follow the same objects through explicit examples. Their purpose is to make algebra, geometry, approximation, and failure modes inspectable. Every numerical illustration retains its stated input and does not replace the corresponding theorem.', [entry('Physics_Foundations_Visual_Atlas', 'Foundations Visual Atlas', 'Packets, currents, reconstruction, and domains'), entry('Physics_Visual_Atlas', 'Dirac Continuum Visual Atlas', 'Spinors, Fourier tails, operator domains, and evidence layers'), entry('Physics_Gauge_Visual_Atlas', 'Gauge Visual Atlas', 'Endpoint covariance, path ordering, and curvature'), entry('Physics_Gravity_Visual_Atlas', 'Gravity Visual Atlas', 'Constraints, reduction, and strong-field diagnostics'), entry('Physics_Adic_Visual_Atlas', 'Adic and Polyphase Visual Atlas', 'Hierarchy, spectral channels, and compatible limits')]), ('VI', 'Verification and computational evidence', 'A proof, a compiler certificate, a numerical check, and a physical interpretation answer different questions. The following appendices identify their exact scope. Source and toolchain identifiers appear here only where they are needed to inspect or reproduce the evidence.', [entry('verification_scope', 'Verification Scope and Source Conventions', 'Mathematical claims, formal coverage, and physical assumptions'), entry('Physics_Foundations_Lean_Companion', 'Foundations Formalization Companion', 'Declarations, dependencies, and the foundations certificate'), entry('Physics_Lean_Companion', 'Dirac Formalization Companion', 'The physical Hamiltonian and its exact source correspondence'), entry('Physics_Gauge_Lean_Companion', 'Gauge Formalization Companion', 'Transport sources, recorded checks, and evidence gaps'), entry('Physics_Gravity_Verification_Companion', 'Gravity Verification Companion', 'Conditional constructions and computational records'), entry('Physics_Adic_Verification_Companion', 'Adic Verification Companion', 'Finite tests and the limits of formal coverage'), entry('Projector_Refinement_Physics_Covariant_Backreaction_Bridge', 'Fiber Model: Computational Evidence', 'Provenance, numerical methods, claims, and parameters', (30, 37)), entry('Projector_Refinement_Physics_Volume_II', 'Cosmology: Reproducibility and Data', 'Source dependencies, reproduction limits, and bibliography', (142, 144))])]
